21
00:00:40,150 --> 00:00:41,960
The story became much bigger.

22
00:00:42,810 --> 00:00:44,760
An aviator, a jeweler, and a

23
00:00:44,770 --> 00:00:46,660
practical idea would become one of

24
00:00:46,670 --> 00:00:48,440
the most recognizable designs in

25
00:00:48,450 --> 00:00:49,120
watchmaking.

26
00:00:49,770 --> 00:00:51,500
But the interesting part isn't just

27
00:00:51,510 --> 00:00:52,920
how the Santos was born.

28
00:00:53,630 --> 00:00:55,280
It's how a flying tool became

29
00:00:55,290 --> 00:00:56,560
a luxury icon.

30
00:00:58,800 --> 00:01:00,730
To understand the watch, start with

31
00:01:00,740 --> 00:01:01,230
the man.

32
00:01:02,160 --> 00:01:04,590
Santos-Dumont was born in Brazil in

33
00:01:04,600 --> 00:01:05,610
eighteen seventy-three.

34
00:01:06,660 --> 00:01:07,890
He grew up around the machinery

35
00:01:07,900 --> 00:01:09,430
of his family's coffee business.

36
00:01:10,320 --> 00:01:12,270
In his own account, engines fascinated

37
00:01:12,280 --> 00:01:14,050
him long before he ever took

38
00:01:14,060 --> 00:01:14,690
to the air.

39
00:01:15,500 --> 00:01:17,090
Paris gave that fascination a much

40
00:01:17,100 --> 00:01:17,970
larger playground.

41
00:01:19,060 --> 00:01:20,110
At the turn of the twentieth

42
00:01:20,120 --> 00:01:21,890
century, he was experimenting with

43
00:01:21,900 --> 00:01:23,610
balloons and powered airships.

44
00:01:24,440 --> 00:01:25,630
These weren't passenger jets.

45
00:01:26,220 --> 00:01:27,430
Think of a long balloon,

46
00:01:28,020 --> 00:01:29,590
an engine, cables, and a pilot

47
00:01:29,600 --> 00:01:30,910
suspended below it.

48
00:01:31,400 --> 00:01:32,530
The city was both his backdrop

49
00:01:32,540 --> 00:01:33,950
and his audience.

50
00:01:34,640 --> 00:01:35,970
That is the world behind the

51
00:01:35,980 --> 00:01:37,890
Santos. Not a polished airport

52
00:01:37,900 --> 00:01:38,450
advertisement.

53
00:01:39,280 --> 00:01:40,410
A world in which flight was

54
00:01:40,420 --> 00:01:41,870
still being worked out in public.

55
00:01:42,580 --> 00:01:44,510
And Santos-Dumont wasn't merely watching

56
00:01:44,520 --> 00:01:45,130
it happen.

57
00:01:45,460 --> 00:01:46,730
He was going up there himself.

58
00:01:49,040 --> 00:01:51,450
In nineteen oh-one, Santos-Dumont flew

59
00:01:51,460 --> 00:01:54,050
his Number Six airship around the

60
00:01:54,060 --> 00:01:56,130
Eiffel Tower and returned to

61
00:01:56,140 --> 00:01:58,470
Saint-Cloud. The challenge behind the

62
00:01:58,480 --> 00:02:00,350
Deutsch Prize was a round trip

63
00:02:00,360 --> 00:02:01,550
