105
00:03:17,460 --> 00:03:19,230
The problem itself does the work.

106
00:03:20,020 --> 00:03:21,430
A watch in a pocket asks

107
00:03:21,440 --> 00:03:22,630
you to retrieve it.

108
00:03:23,100 --> 00:03:24,190
A watch on your wrist is

109
00:03:24,200 --> 00:03:25,750
already waiting where you can glance

110
00:03:25,760 --> 00:03:26,390
at it.

111
00:03:27,000 --> 00:03:28,070
It's the sort of change that

112
00:03:28,080 --> 00:03:29,770
looks obvious after somebody has made

113
00:03:29,780 --> 00:03:30,130
it.

114
00:03:30,780 --> 00:03:32,530
But obvious solutions can be the

115
00:03:32,540 --> 00:03:34,110
ones that travel furthest.

116
00:03:34,760 --> 00:03:36,350
Cartier had given a practical need

117
00:03:36,360 --> 00:03:38,270
a form people could recognize.

118
00:03:40,800 --> 00:03:42,070
Now look at the design again.

119
00:03:42,800 --> 00:03:44,350
The square outline gives the dial

120
00:03:44,360 --> 00:03:44,890
a frame.

121
00:03:45,580 --> 00:03:47,090
The numerals make it feel formal.

122
00:03:47,740 --> 00:03:49,430
The visible screws give it an

123
00:03:49,440 --> 00:03:51,470
